https://opencollective.com/redux-form/contributors.svg

The badge is relying on the result of this GraphQL query:

```
query Collective($collectiveSlug: String) {
  Collective(slug: $collectiveSlug) {
    id
    data
  }
}
```

Which is returning nothing:

```
{
  "data": {
    "Collective": {
      "id": 18332,
      "data": {}
    }
  }
}
```

The `update-contributions' cron job is supposed to take care of that. Let's run it:

`heroku run npx babel-node cron/daily/update-contributions.js --app opencollective-prod-api`

We're getting an error:

```
/app/node_modules/bluebird/js/release/debuggability.js:113
        throw new Error("cannot enable long stack traces after promises have been created\u000a\u000a    See http://goo.gl/MqrFmX\u000a");
        ^
Error: cannot enable long stack traces after promises have been created
```
